### Dhaka Tesla Pool: the story as runnable HTTP calls.
### Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each call, in order.
### Start the API first: `docker compose up -d db` (repo root), then `npm run dev` (apps/api).
### Cookies are remembered between calls, so signing in as someone makes the next calls theirs.
### To replay from scratch: `docker compose down -v`, `docker compose up -d db`, `npm run db:migrate`, `npm run db:seed`.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@password = banani0841

### Is everything up?
GET http://localhost:4000/health

### What Nusrat's trip will cost before she books (৳100 solo, ৳75 pooled)
GET {{api}}/fares/estimate?pickup=BANANI&dropoff=MOHAKHALI

### ── 08:41, Banani Road 11. Jashim goes online with Bullet ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jashim@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
PATCH {{api}}/driver/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{ "online": true, "zone": "BANANI" }

### ── Nusrat books Banani → Mohakhali (no trip exists yet, so she waits) ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nusrat@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name nusratBooks
POST {{api}}/rides
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pickupZone": "BANANI", "dropoffZone": "MOHAKHALI", "seats": 1 }

### ── Jashim sees her waiting and accepts: this creates Bullet's pool ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jashim@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
GET {{api}}/driver/requests

###
# @name acceptNusrat
POST {{api}}/driver/requests/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}/accept

### ── Two minutes later Rafiq books Banani → Gulshan 1: he joins Bullet instantly (auto-join) ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rafiq@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name rafiqBooks
POST {{api}}/rides
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pickupZone": "BANANI", "dropoffZone": "GULSHAN_1", "seats": 1 }

### Rafiq tries to look at Nusrat's ride: 404, as if it didn't exist
GET {{api}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}

### ── 30 seconds later Shirin books Banani → Tejgaon: 4 km from Gulshan 1, so she waits ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "shirin@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name shirinBooks
POST {{api}}/rides
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pickupZone": "BANANI", "dropoffZone": "TEJGAON", "seats": 1 }

### Her timeline says why she wasn't matched (SEAT_CLAIM_REJECTED, DROPOFF_TOO_FAR)
GET {{api}}/rides/{{shirinBooks.response.body.ride.id}}

### ── Jashim: arrive, start (fares lock at ৳75 and ৳90), drop Nusrat, then Rafiq ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jashim@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
POST {{api}}/pools/{{acceptNusrat.response.body.pool.id}}/arrive

###
POST {{api}}/pools/{{acceptNusrat.response.body.pool.id}}/start

###
POST {{api}}/pools/{{acceptNusrat.response.body.pool.id}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}/drop-off

###
POST {{api}}/pools/{{acceptNusrat.response.body.pool.id}}/rides/{{rafiqBooks.response.body.ride.id}}/drop-off

### Jashim's finished trips (collected ৳165)
GET {{api}}/driver/pools?scope=history

### ── Nusrat looks back: what exactly happened? ──
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nusrat@teslapool.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
GET {{api}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}
